INT. PARKING STRUCTURE, LEVEL P4 - NIGHT

Concrete ramps spiral up into the dark. Sodium lights hum. Rain falls through the open side of the structure and pools in the drains.

A black sedan idles at the far end, headlights off.

KAZIMIERZ "KAZ" DRAGOMIR (40s, black overcoat, a briefcase handcuffed to his wrist) stands beside it, checking his watch. A step behind him, his driver, LEOPOLDINA "LEO" MARCHETTI (30s, earpiece, one hand inside her jacket).

A second car rolls up the ramp. Stops. Its doors open.

AGENT CALLUM BRIGHTWATER (30s, FBI windbreaker under a coat) climbs out, followed by AGENT PRIYA RAMAKRISHNAN (30s, a notebook she isn't writing in) and a third man, a CONSULTANT named OSWALD PELL (60s, cardigan, cane).

KAZ
You're early, Agent Brightwater.

CALLUM
You're late, Mr. Dragomir.

LEO
Kaz, we should go.

KAZ
We're fine, Leo.

PRIYA
(low, to Callum)
Cal, where's the exchange?

CALLUM
Be patient, Pri.

OSWALD
(under his breath)
There is no exchange.

Priya turns to stare at him. Callum's hand closes slowly on the grip of his sidearm.

PRIYA
Say that again.

OSWALD
The briefcase is empty, my dear. It's always been empty.

KAZ
(over him)
That's a lie --

LEO
Kaz, he's --

CALLUM
Everybody, hands where I can see them!

KAZ
(shouting)
Leo, don't!

LEO ^
(shouting)
Drop it, Brightwater!

CALLUM
Priya, back off!

PRIYA
Cal, I'm not --

A dozen heartbeats. Rain drums. Then Oswald taps his cane twice on the concrete, almost courteously.

OSWALD
Thirty seconds.

Above them, engines start. Headlights flare on every level, blinding, a cathedral of white. Dozens of silhouettes line the railings. A bullhorn crackles.

BULLHORN (V.O.)
Federal agents. Drop your weapons.

PRIYA
Cal, those aren't ours.

CALLUM
Whose are they?

OSWALD
(smiling)
Mine.

Kaz laughs. It is a short, cracked laugh. He unlocks the handcuff, opens the briefcase, and tilts it toward them. Inside: a single brass key.

KAZ
Gentlemen, ladies. Last chance to leave.

Nobody moves. Leo steps toward Priya. Callum keeps his gun on Oswald.

PRIYA
(to Leo)
Who do you work for?

LEO
Whoever pays.

CALLUM
(to Oswald)
And you?

OSWALD
Whoever pays more.

The headlights go dark all at once. Gunfire.
